{title: The LORD Is My Shepherd}
{subtitle: Psalm 23}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]The LORD is my shep[Bb]herd
I lack [F/A]nothing
He lets me lie [Gm]down in green [Eb]pastures
He leads me be[Bb]side still waters
He restores [F/A]my soul
He [Gm]guides me along [F]right [Eb]paths
For his name's [Bb]sake
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]The LORD is my shep[Bb]herd
I lack noth[F/A]ing
The LORD is my shep[Gm]herd
I lack noth[Eb]ing
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Even though I walk through the valley of the [F/A]shadow of death
[Gm]I fear no evil, [Eb]for you are with me
[Bb]Your rod and your staff, they comfort [F/A]me
You set [Gm]a table before me in [Eb]the presence of my enemies
[Bb]You anoint my head with [F/A]oil
My cup over[Gm]flows
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]The LORD is my [Bb]shepherd
I lack [F/A]nothing
The LORD is my [Gm]shepherd
I lack noth[Eb]ing
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]Surely goodness and mer[F/A]cy will pursue me
[Gm]All the days of my life
And [Eb]I [Bb]will dwell in the house of the [F/A]LORD
For length of [Gm]days
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The LORD is [Eb]my shepherd
I lack noth[Bb]ing
The LORD is my shep[F/A]herd
I lack nothing
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
